                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.34119/1434: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-01T11:00:00-04:00">July 1, 1938—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:56 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>175. From Braden. My 174, June 30, 8 p.m., first paragraph. Argentine Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs informed me last night the proposed meeting with the chiefs
                    of mission would be postponed for a few days until assurances can be obtained
                    from Chile and Peru that they will at least endeavor to discover some means
                    within their treaty obligations with Bolivia which would permit them to enforce
                    as rigid neutrality regulations in the event of another war, as Argentina,
                    Brazil and Uruguay could with Paraguay and the United States with both
                    ex-belligerent nations. Argentine Minister for Foreign Affairs thus desired
                    uniformity of action by the six mediatory powers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
